        "original_id": "f4615d2b-4d49-515a-ade8-d54d5693a33e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Model 17 grenade, Kugelhandgranate, Stielhandgranate, Stick grenade\n- Concepts: portability, handling, appearance, nicknames, infantry weapons\n\nFacts:\n- The Model 17 grenade was more portable than the heavier Kugelhandgranate.\n- The Model 17 grenade was less awkward to handle than the Stick grenade.\n- The Stielhandgranate had a very distinctive appearance.\n- The Stielhandgranate was called a \"stick grenade\" and \"potato masher\" in British Army slang because of its appearance.\n- The Stielhandgranate is now one of the most easily recognized infantry weapons of the 20th century.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
